{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DeprovisionPolicy","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" is never written: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses it locally, before any request, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation failure (CONTRACT.md §34.2 P12.2, contract 1.60 A4) — never as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\""},{"type":"text","text":", never left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the server to refuse. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DeprovisionPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK17DeprovisionPolicyO","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","title":"DeprovisionPolicy","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DeprovisionPolicy","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What happens downstream to a user who falls out of scope or is no longer active. Erasure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always deletes, whatever this says."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/deactivate","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/delete","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/unknown"],"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/init(from:)-sf4y","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/init(rawValue:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/encode(to:)"],"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DeprovisionPolicy\/RawRepresentable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/deprovisionpolicy"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Axi